[4;35mNAME[0m                                                                            

[1mcatalog [0m— concatenate and number files                                          

[4;35mSYNOPSIS[0m                                                                        

[1mcatalog [0m[[1m-bn[0m] [[1m-o [0m[3moutput[0m] [[3mfile ...[0m]                                            

[4;35mDESCRIPTION[0m                                                                     

The [1mcatalog [0mutility reads each [3mfile [0min turn and writes it to the standard       
output. The options are as follows:                                             

[1m-b[0m
    Number the non-blank lines.                                                 

[1m-o [0m[1;3moutput[0m
    Write to [3moutput [0minstead of “standard output”.                               

[4;35mEXAMPLES[0m                                                                        

[48;2;43;48;59m                                                                                [0m
[48;2;43;48;59m [0m[38;2;192;197;206;48;2;43;48;59m$ catalog -n notes.txt[0m[48;2;43;48;59m                                                        [0m[48;2;43;48;59m [0m
[48;2;43;48;59m                                                                                [0m

[4;35mEXIT STATUS[0m                                                                     

The [1mcatalog[0m utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.              

